, B., D.T. Liu, H. Yao, D. Bartsch, E.R. Kandel, S.A. Siegelbaum, and G.R. Tibbs. <year>1998</year>. Identification of a gene encoding a hyperpolarization-activated pacemaker channel of brain. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>93</volume>:<fpage>717</fpage>&#x02013;729.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9630217</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Seed, B., and A. Aruffo. <year>1987</year>. Molecular cloning of the CD2 antigen, the T-cell erythrocyte receptor, by a rapid immunoselection procedure. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>84</volume>:<fpage>3365</fpage>&#x02013;3369.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2437578</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Shin, K.S., B.S. Rothberg, and G. Yellen. <year>2001</year>. Blocker state dependence and trapping in hyperpolarization-activated cation channels: evidence for an intracellular activation gate. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>117</volume>:<fpage>91</fpage>&#x02013;101.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11158163</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>